<details class="panel overview-explanation"><summary>Sources and coverage limits</summary><p>Independent checks and backup heartbeat are existing GitHub workflows. No new monitoring service, schedule or notification is created. At most two fixed public GitHub GET requests run per refresh, each with a three-second timeout and one-MiB response limit. A rate-limited or unavailable source remains unknown.</p><p>Successful encrypted backup requires a matching unexpired retained artifact. Component restore acceptance comes from live V1-023; full incident recovery comes from live V1-014. Monitor-only workflow success is never counted as a restore. Website/configuration archive freshness is not connected here; use the accepted recovery task for its historical evidence. No raw logs, customer payloads, tokens or private backup files are exposed.</p></details>
